      "description": {
        "en": "The Amazon Fire TV Stick 4K Plus (2025) adds streaming apps to a television with an HDMI port, suiting viewers who want modern streaming without replacing their TV. It supports 4K output, Dolby Vision, HDR10+, Dolby Atmos and Wi-Fi 6, with an included Alexa Voice Remote for voice search and basic TV control.\n\nIts quad-core processor runs at up to 1.7GHz, while 8GB of internal storage accommodates core streaming apps but leaves limited room for larger app collections or games. The television and chosen service must support the relevant 4K or HDR format. Wi-Fi 6 helps most when paired with a compatible router and stable broadband. Subscriptions are not bundled, and cloud gaming may require a separate subscription and compatible controller. Alexa+ features and individual apps can vary by region.\n\nAt a recently reported deal price near $37.99, it is a compelling midrange option for 4K households wanting Dolby Vision and Atmos without stepping up to the 4K Max. Owners of 1080p-only TVs may prefer a simpler, cheaper streamer, while users needing more storage should compare alternatives. Check the live price, regional app availability and TV compatibility before ordering.",
