        "en": "The Keurig K-Express is a single-serve coffee maker designed for people who want a fresh cup without brewing an entire carafe or navigating complicated settings. Its straightforward buttons select 8, 10, or 12 oz servings, while the Strong Brew option is intended to produce a bolder-tasting cup. That makes it a practical fit for individual morning routines, small kitchens, and office coffee stations where convenience matters more than extensive customization.\n\nThe removable 42 oz reservoir holds about 1.24 liters of water and supports up to four 8 oz cups before refilling. Removing the drip tray creates space for a travel mug up to 7.4 inches tall. The machine primarily uses K-Cup pods, but ground coffee is also possible with the compatible My K-Cup reusable filter, which is sold separately. The listed version operates at 120 volts, and its auto-off feature switches the brewer off five minutes after the last brew.\n\nThis model makes sense for buyers who value speed, simple controls, and adjustable serving sizes. It is not a traditional espresso machine and does not froth milk or offer advanced temperature control. Running costs also depend on pod prices and availability, so frequent coffee drinkers who prefer ground coffee may find another brewing style more economical.",
